#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "zendesk.api"

Feature: Notification Routing
	Testing the notification routing of specific tickets

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails

Teardown:
	* I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown users with the following userExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| User1  |
	| Agent1 |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds from zendesk.liferay.com
	| 12345678 |
	#Necessary pause after the teardown and the next test execution
	* I wait for "3" seconds

Scenario: Notify requester of received request
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	End users who create requests for specific products should receive a notification that the request was sent.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved            |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1 |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                |
	| Shared Comments  | true                |
	| SLA              | Gold                |
	| Tier             | T4                  |
	| Support Region   | US                  |
	| Support Language | English             |
	| External ID      | 12345678            |
	And I assign an organization with organizationExternalId "12345678" with the following tags
	| developer_tools         |
	| enterprise_search       |
	| liferay_analytics_cloud |
	| liferay_commerce        |
	| liferay_dxp             |
	| lxc_sm                  |
	| management_tools_lcs    |
	| mobile_device_detection |
	| mobile_experience       |
	| productivity_tools_sync |
	| social_office           |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | ${staticZendeskAdminPassword}    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)       |
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following product and component values
	| prd_developer_tools         |                                       |
	| prd_enterprise_search       | monitoring                            |
	| prd_liferay_analytics_cloud |                                       |
	| prd_liferay_commerce_1_1    | activation_key_project_administration |
	| prd_liferay_commerce_2_0    | commerce_insights                     |
	| prd_liferay_commerce_2_1    | configuration_and_settings            |
	| prd_liferay_commerce_3_0    | connectors                            |
	| prd_liferay_commerce_4_0    | digital_merchandise_management        |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_4         | authentication                        |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_3         | caching_clustering                    |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_2         | calendar                              |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_1         | collaboration                         |
	| prd_liferay_dxp_7_0         | content_management                    |
	| prd_lxc_sm                  | backup_recovery                       |
	| prd_management_tools_lcs    |                                       |
	| prd_mobile_device_detection |                                       |
	| prd_mobile_experience       |                                       |
	| prd_productivity_tools_sync |                                       |
	| prd_social_office           |                                       |
	Then emails regarding the reception of the following ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" for the support language "English" with the following parameters should be sent out
	| Recipients | Zendesk User1                                                                                                                    |
	| Subject    | [Liferay Support] {{ticket.organization.name}} {{ticket.id}}: {{ticket.title}}                                                   |
	| Body       | Hello {{ticket.requester.first_name}}                                                                                            |
	| Body       | Thank you for contacting the Liferay Support Team regarding your {{ticket.organization.name}} project                            |
	| Body       | At this time, one of our Customer Support Engineers is carefully reviewing your request                                          |
	| Body       | {{ticket.id}})                                                                                                                   |
	| Body       | and will be responding shortly                                                                                                   |
	| Body       | Please be sure that you have included all relevant information or attachments and if applicable, steps to reproduce the behavior |
	| Body       | Regards                                                                                                                          |
	| Body       | Liferay Support                                                                                                                  |
	And "6.2" legacy ticket emails related to the following ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" for the support language "English" should not be sent out
	And "6.1" legacy ticket emails related to the following ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" for the support language "English" should not be sent out
	And "6.0" legacy ticket emails related to the following ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" for the support language "English" should not be sent out
	And "5.2" legacy ticket emails related to the following ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" for the support language "English" should not be sent out

Scenario: Notify requester of received request and 62 EOSL Policy
	End users who create requests for Liferay Portal 6.2 should receive a notification that the request was sent as well as information on the 6.2 EOSL policy.

	Given I create an organization with the following values
	| Status           | Approved            |
	| Name             | Organization Name 1 |
	| Tags             | liferay_portal      |
	| Shared Tickets   | true                |
	| Shared Comments  | true                |
	| SLA              | Gold                |
	| Tier             | T4                  |
	| Support Region   | US                  |
	| Support Language | English             |
	| External ID      | 12345678            |
	And I create a user with the following values
	| Name             | Zendesk User1                    |
	| Tags             | osb_customer,osb_kb              |
	| Password         | ${staticZendeskAdminPassword}    |
	| Role             | End-user                         |
	| Access           | Organization                     |
	| Email            | zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken |
	| Phone Number     | +1 (555) 555-5555                |
	| Organization     | Organization Name 1              |
	| Language         | English                          |
	| Time Zone        | Pacific Time (US & Canada)       |
	| External ID      | User1                            |
	When I create several requests as a user with the email address "zendesk.user1@zendesk.com.broken" with the following product and component values
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_2 | activation_key_project_administration |
	| prd_liferay_portal_6_2 | authentication                        |
	Then emails regarding the reception of the following "6.2" ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" for the support language "English" with the following parameters should be sent out
	| Recipients | Zendesk User1                                                                                                                      |
	| Subject    | [Liferay Support] {{ticket.organization.name}} {{ticket.id}}: {{ticket.title}}                                                     |
	| Body       | Hello {{ticket.requester.first_name}}                                                                                              |
	| Body       | Thank you for contacting the Liferay Support Team                                                                                  |
	| Body       | At this time, one of our Customer Support Engineers is carefully reviewing your request                                            |
	| Body       | {{ticket.id}})                                                                                                                     |
	| Body       | and will be responding shortly                                                                                                     |	
	| Body       | Please note, however, that the Premium Support Phase for Liferay Portal 6.2 EE has passed and your support services may be limited |
	| Body       | Please review our End of Service Life Policy and reach out to your sales representative for available options                      |
	| Body       | Regards                                                                                                                            |
	| Body       | Liferay Support                                                                                                                    |
	And non-legacy ticket emails related to the following ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" for the support language "English" should not be sent out

